<section style="padding:72px 24px 40px;"><div style="max-width:860px;margin:0 auto;"><div class="rich"><p>Land surveying in the Adelaide Hills and Mount Barker usually starts with a practical question. Where is the boundary, what levels does the designer need, or can this block be divided at all? The Greater Adelaide Regional Plan puts the Adelaide Hills and Mount Barker District councils in one land supply region. It names Mount Barker as the largest urban area there.</p><p>Torrens Survey Co is an advertising and introduction service. It doesn't carry out surveys. It puts you in touch with an independent Licensed Surveyor, who quotes and contracts with you directly. In South Australia, only licensed surveyors can undertake a boundary survey or place a survey mark that defines a property boundary (Surveyors Board SA), so check any surveyor's licence on the Surveyors Board register before you agree to anything. Not sure which survey you need? Call (08) 5550 3814 and start there.</p></div></div></section>
<section style="padding:0 24px 64px;"><div style="max-width:1100px;margin:0 auto;">
    <span class="kicker">What We Do in Adelaide Hills & Mount Barker</span>
    <h2 class="section-heading" style="font-size:clamp(22px,3vw,32px);margin:0 0 28px;">Services for Adelaide Hills & Mount Barker Properties</h2>
    <div class="feat-grid" style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,1fr);gap:20px;">
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #E4DFD4;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(14,77,110,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Instrument Sans',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:700;color:#111418;margin:0 0 8px;">Boundary surveys</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">For a fence going up or coming down, or when the pegs have gone. A fence line doesn't show the legal boundary. Only a Licensed Surveyor can determine it.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #E4DFD4;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(14,77,110,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Instrument Sans',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:700;color:#111418;margin:0 0 8px;">Feature and level surveys</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">The usual way to get the existing levels and boundary offsets a site plan needs, which matters when a designer is drawing a house or extension on a block with a fall.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #E4DFD4;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(14,77,110,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Instrument Sans',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:700;color:#111418;margin:0 0 8px;">Land division surveys</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">Thinking about splitting a block in the Hills or Mount Barker? A Licensed Surveyor works alongside the council, planning consent and Land Services SA steps that come before new titles issue.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #E4DFD4;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(14,77,110,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Instrument Sans',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:700;color:#111418;margin:0 0 8px;">Identification surveys</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">Buying a house, shed or rural-living property? An identification survey is how owners check for encroachments involving neighbouring properties before they buy or sell.</p>
      </div>
</div>
<style>
